1
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:28,170
Huh?

2
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,620
Oh, whew.

3
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:54,340
It was just a dream.

4
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:58,290
Boy, that was scary.

5
00:00:58,290 --> 00:01:01,230
Father had been killed.

6
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:06,400
I wandered across battlefields
fighting men who were like monsters.

7
00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:09,500
And in the end, I became a slave.

8
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:19,040
I'm glad I'm here.

9
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,600
It's so peaceful.

10
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,930
What's with this guy?

11
00:01:46,930 --> 00:01:49,350
H-He's so persistent.

12
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:53,770
Stay down already!

13
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:59,180
Damn it.

14
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:06,800
What's wrong? I'll keep fighting.

15
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:17,300
Let's find out if we're beneath you or not!

16
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,480
I don't have time for this.

17
00:02:27,050 --> 00:02:31,010
Aw, man. I've had enough.

18
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:36,270
You'd better prepare yourselves.

19
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:43,180
You slaves have got some serious punishment
waiting for you after going this wild.

20
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:58,030
We won.

21
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:40,390
Oath

22
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:56,600
Father!

23
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,610
Listen to this.

24
00:05:03,610 --> 00:05:06,060
I just had a crazy dream.

25
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,880
A bunch of arrows came flying, and you—

26
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:12,130
I smell blood.

27
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:13,920
Huh?

28
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:17,700
Who did you kill...

29
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,480
with that knife?

30
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:24,840
What?

31
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:10,240
It was to protect you.

32
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,820
That strength was for protecting you.

33
00:06:18,970 --> 00:06:21,660
I'm sorry, Thorfinn.

34
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:26,580
I still had things to tell you.

35
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:31,620
There was still so much
I needed to teach you.

36
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:39,940
No. Father...

37
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:45,770
I... This is...

38
00:06:46,110 --> 00:06:47,560
I'm sorry...

39
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:49,770
I did this!

40
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:52,790
...for leaving you alone.

41
00:06:52,790 --> 00:06:57,450
Father, wait! Wait! Father!

42
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:03,250
You understand now.

43
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:08,700
You don't have any enemies.

44
00:07:09,370 --> 00:07:12,940
Nobody has any enemies.

45
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:34,740
There's no one who it's okay to hurt.

46
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,920
There never was.

47
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:11,300
What is this place? Valhalla?

48
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:47,140
They're laughing...

49
00:10:11,020 --> 00:10:12,120
Bjorn?

50
00:10:25,690 --> 00:10:30,880
Still stuck up there, huh, Thorfinn?

51
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:44,390
Hey. It's been a while.

52
00:10:57,690 --> 00:11:00,080
Askeladd...

53
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:05,750
You never learn, do you?

54
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:08,030
You're already back here again?

55
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:15,640
Is this Valhalla?

56
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:21,380
What? Valhalla?

57
00:11:28,690 --> 00:11:30,920
You think this is the afterlife?

58
00:11:31,490 --> 00:11:33,540
You can't be serious.

59
00:11:34,130 --> 00:11:36,560
The afterlife is a much nicer place than this.

60
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:39,770
Look carefully.

61
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:44,560
This place is no different
from the world of the living.

62
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:49,940
It's where all the shit gets dumped...

63
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:56,040
Where all warriors wind up.

64
00:11:58,700 --> 00:12:01,360
It's the purest form of war.

65
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:08,260
There is no victory. There is no end.

66
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:13,780
In this place, everyone besides
yourself is your enemy.

67
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:22,420
Everyone... is your enemy...

68
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:27,530
Do you remember, Thorfinn?

69
00:12:28,050 --> 00:12:33,120
You used to live here with us.

70
00:12:34,690 --> 00:12:41,800
But for better or for worse, you became empty.

71
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:52,280
That's why you were able
to escape this place.

72
00:12:54,930 --> 00:13:01,380
I shouldn't be saying this as the man
who dragged you here, but you're lucky.

73
00:13:02,450 --> 00:13:06,460
Not many men ever manage to escape.

74
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,880
Just look at Bjorn.

75
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:23,720
You were once filled with the idea of being
a warrior, but then you were emptied out.

76
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:27,460
What's inside you now?

77
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:37,760
I'm... still a warrior.

78
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:44,760
I struck someone in a fit of rage.

79
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:48,860
That's why I'm back here.

80
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,500
I still reside in this place.

81
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:58,950
My hands are about to give out, too.

82
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:07,660
I'm pathetic. I never grow.

83
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:12,850
Me, me, me.

84
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:18,390
Good grief. A little soul-searching is all well
and good, but try to keep your eyes open.

85
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:27,000
Something terrifying's
right beneath your feet.

86
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:48,380
You're kicking them? How cruel.

87
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:54,130
Shouldn't you lend an ear to their complaints?

88
00:14:54,830 --> 00:14:55,860
Complaints?

89
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:59,990
That's right. Look closely.

90
00:14:59,990 --> 00:15:02,140
I'm sure you recognize some of those faces.

91
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:09,120
They're all of the people you killed.

92
00:15:12,610 --> 00:15:13,390
What?

93
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:22,840
I...

94
00:15:56,760 --> 00:16:01,760
You... All of you...

95
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:08,080
I don't know who you are
or where you're from.

96
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:18,960
I can't remember where or when I killed you.

97
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:47,440
I'm sorry.

98
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:12,860
Unbelievable. What an uncouth lot.

99
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:23,050
Come on! You don't have time to cry.

100
00:17:23,050 --> 00:17:25,950
You don't want to fall back
down here, do you?

101
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:31,960
Even if they're hanging off you, keep climbing!

102
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:34,220
Climb!

103
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:42,420
That's your battle.

104
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:52,460
Go!

105
00:17:53,950 --> 00:17:56,910
Take the people you killed with you!

106
00:17:57,830 --> 00:18:00,650
Fight your true battle!

107
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:03,840
Become a true warrior,

108
00:18:04,530 --> 00:18:06,100
Thorfinn!

109
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:53,740
A dream?

110
00:18:58,060 --> 00:18:59,520
A true...

111
00:19:16,650 --> 00:19:18,700
Einar. Einar!

112
00:19:19,130 --> 00:19:21,130
Hey! Are you alive?

113
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:30,240
Yeah.

114
00:19:32,130 --> 00:19:36,300
We won the fight.

115
00:19:44,330 --> 00:19:47,060
Man, we've hit rock bottom.

116
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:54,420
We're drowning in debt, our wheat
has been ruined, and I'm a mess.

117
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:59,370
On top of that, we'll be punished
for getting into that fight.

118
00:20:02,650 --> 00:20:09,450
But seeing you punch
that guy sure was satisfying.

119
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:13,080
Ow...

120
00:20:15,850 --> 00:20:19,050
What's wrong? Are you in pain, too?

121
00:20:29,170 --> 00:20:39,080
Einar, I've used these hands
to kill so many people.

122
00:20:42,210 --> 00:20:45,240
People no different from your family...

123
00:20:47,410 --> 00:20:49,410
People whose names I didn't even know.

124
00:20:50,890 --> 00:20:53,180
People who I bore no grudge against.

125
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:09,380
And today, I struck another person.

126
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:17,090
But it ends now.

127
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:25,570
I'll never hurt anyone again.

128
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:30,280
As of today, I'm swearing off violence.

129
00:21:31,970 --> 00:21:33,450
I'm going to be reborn.

130
00:21:34,650 --> 00:21:38,300
I need to be reborn and
start atoning for what I've done.

131
00:21:57,880 --> 00:22:03,840
I'm going to fight my true battle.

132
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:11,060
I see. All right.

133
00:22:12,130 --> 00:22:16,320
I don't really get it,
but I hear you loud and clear.

134
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:23,540
I'm going to be reborn.

135
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:37,180
They're not going to be punished?
That's ridiculous!

136
00:22:37,510 --> 00:22:41,930
Master, this matter concerns
order and discipline on the farm!

137
00:22:44,410 --> 00:22:49,190
Pater found this on the
ravaged farm this morning.

138
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:57,030
By the way, Trygve,
where's that coat you always wear?

139
00:22:57,030 --> 00:22:59,570
Huh? What? Uh...

140
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:04,890
The farm was ravaged by wild boars.
There was no fight.

141
00:23:04,890 --> 00:23:09,130
That's the story we're going with. Got it?

142
00:23:13,120 --> 00:23:16,180
Thank you, master.

143
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:20,920
You're a strong man, Pater.

144
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:24,980
You're not the slightest bit afraid of being
ostracized by the people you work with?

145
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:27,800
I've been through a lot.

146
00:23:28,480 --> 00:23:30,880
After all, I used to be a slave.

147
00:23:32,970 --> 00:23:35,800
Loosen up or you'll wear yourself out.

148
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:38,610
Let the weight of the hoe do the work.

149
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:42,840
Yes, sir.

150
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:39,900
The Cursed Head

151
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:39,000
"The Cursed Head."
